  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>Walton-on-Thames railway station serves Walton-on-Thames and north Hersham in Surrey. Platform 1 is used by trains towards London Waterloo. Platform 2 is used by trains towards Weybridge, Woking and destinations farther west and south-west, including selected services to Guildford, Basingstoke and Portsmouth Harbour.</p>

        <p>The station is on the South West Main Line, approximately 17.1 miles by rail from London Waterloo. South Western Railway manages the station and operates its passenger services. The station code is <strong>WAL</strong>. The station has four platforms in total; Platforms 1 and 2 are operational, while the other two, beside the central fast lines, are out of use, gated and inaccessible.</p>

        <figure>
          <img src="/images/station/walton-on-thames-station-sign.webp" alt="The National Rail double arrow totem sign reading Walton-on-Thames, mounted on a post in front of the station's brick boundary wall" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
          <figcaption>The National Rail totem at Walton-on-Thames station. Photograph by Darren Bayley, 25 August 2026.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p><a href="https://www.nationalrail.co.uk/live-trains/departures/walton-on-thames/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check live departures from Walton-on-Thames ↗</a></p>

        <blockquote>
          <p><strong>Checked against National Rail and South Western Railway:</strong> August 2026. Always check live running information for the day you're travelling, since this page can't reflect disruption or timetable changes in real time.</p>
